WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.130
Our school put a word filter on

2
00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:04.430
its chatbot: block any message

3
00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:05.650
with “password” in it.

4
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.650
Within a week, a scam got through anyway.

5
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.300
It asked pupils for “your

6
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.700
login code” instead.

7
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.230
Today: the rules we put around a

8
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.950
model, and which ones hold.

9
00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.230
A guardrail is a rule around

10
00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:23.430
the model, not inside it.

11
00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.490
There are three main kinds.

12
00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.210
A filter on what goes in.

13
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.810
A filter on what comes out.

14
00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.550
And a check on what the AI is about to do.

15
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.140
Filters are often word lists.

16
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.400
They catch the plain version:

17
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:41.780
“send me your password”.

18
00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.930
But a reworded message, with no word on

19
00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.710
the list, walks straight past.

20
00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:50.130
And in Arabic or Hausa, the

21
00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:51.610
list may not even exist.

22
00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:55.710
Word lists also block innocent things.

23
00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.980
A lesson on choosing a strong

24
00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:00.220
password gets stopped, just

25
00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.100
because it says “password”.

26
00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:05.110
So filters miss attacks and stop the

27
00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:07.130
innocent: two kinds of mistake.

28
00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.040
Quick check!

29
00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:13.450
Our filter blocks the word “password”.

30
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.420
A message asks pupils to

31
00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.980
“share your login code”.

32
00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:20.250
What happens?

33
00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:24.190
It gets past: no word from the list.

34
00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.750
Now the guardrail that holds.

35
00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.640
Before the AI sends anything, code

36
00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.660
asks: did a person ask for this, and

37
00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.380
say yes to this exact message?

38
00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.710
However it's worded, an

39
00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.670
unapproved message doesn't go.

40
00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:42.070
Think of the school gate.

41
00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.630
A list of banned faces misses anyone new.

42
00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.240
A rule that only people with a pass

43
00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.800
get in works whoever comes.

44
00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.100
Check what's allowed, not

45
00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.080
just what's banned.

46
00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.000
No single guardrail is

47
00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.020
perfect, so use layers.

48
00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:01.810
Picture slices of cheese, each with holes.

49
00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.220
One slice lets things through; stack

50
00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:07.800
several, and the holes rarely line up.

51
00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:10.910
In the app, send a scam message

52
00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:12.490
through three guardrails.

53
00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.220
Catch it with plain words, then reword it

54
00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.300
and watch it slip past the filter.

55
00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:21.160
Then switch on the check in code.

56
00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.170
Your turn.

57
00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.430
Which guardrail stops a message nobody

58
00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.490
approved, however it's worded?

59
00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:31.190
The check in code: it

60
00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:32.510
doesn't care about wording.

61
00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.130
Remember: guardrails are

62
00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.430
rules around the model.

63
00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:38.950
Word lists miss rewording

64
00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.430
and stop the innocent.

65
00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:43.850
Check the action, allow rather than

66
00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.430
just ban, and stack layers.

67
00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:49.170
Try it in class tomorrow:

68
00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:51.670
build a “word-list robot”.

69
00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.560
One pupil holds a list of banned

70
00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.500
words and checks every message.

71
00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:59.080
Classmates reword a harmless

72
00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.420
message to get past.

73
00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.500
Then add a teacher who must approve

74
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.180
each message, and compare.
